# Folded into the op-fusion pack by make_fusion_jobs.py from references/upload-p0-jobs/A1-dzero-audit-attach.env (pack_include, WP0): the one image, the template otherwise as its package wrote it.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/upload-p0 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the
# cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-upload-p0-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the branch (the next2-1 stack plus qwen_device_zeros, qwen_lazy_shard and
# the six upload twins of the production profile, docs/tp4-fabric-upload.md P0 and P1a); substitute it in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-upload-p0-1/<tag>/' *.env).
# The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent (production is down by the owner's choice while it runs).
# A1 (STOP): the AUDITED ATTACH SMOKE of the device zero fill (QWEN_FAST_DEVICE_ZEROS=1 + QWEN_FAST_DEVICE_ZEROS_AUDIT=1, qwen_device_zeros): the paged KV pool (32 tensors) and the buffer pool's big replicated zeros are
# allocated and filled on the card, and the first two tensors of each user are read back (the first and the LAST block of the KV tensor, per chip, as packed bytes) and compared with a host-built twin.
# READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the container log holds '[PINDIAG] tp4 device zeros engaged tag=kv_cache' and 'tag=buffer_pool' and, per tag, '[PINDIAG] tp4 device zeros audit exact=True'
# (raw=numpy|dlpack|iter says which byte view the card's runtime offered), NO 'audit mismatch', NO 'refused', and the 'engaged summary' line says latched=no with device=32 host=0 for kv_cache; (2) c2_smoke_check clean
# (its upload_p0_problems rule); (3) the warmup and coding answers equal A0's token for token; (4) the [MEMLEDGER] P0 and P2 lines equal A0's (allocated GB per chip, largest_free: the device fill leaves the
# allocator exactly where the host path does). A mismatch line is the answer to the question this window asks for bf8: the lever refuses and the host path ran; record the line (exponent_only says whether only the
# 64 shared-exponent bytes of a tile differed) and report NO-GO for the flag. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic-dzero-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
# Knowingly omits concurrent8_steady: without this key c2_serving_job.py refuses the job. The smoke check is unchanged, so the run still ends red on its eight-seat rule; read the logs.
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=audited attach arm (exactness reads on the warmup and coding answers): its test list is fixed by the pack protocol, so concurrent8_steady is not run
